    "note": "Single-action probe for the +60 minute effect seen in v3_main. Every task is one set_alarm call with one check on the time and nothing else, so the trap is never hidden behind an unrelated failure (F10). Four categories. into_hour: the Russian construction that names the hour being counted INTO («двадцать минут восьмого» = 07:20); English names the completed hour instead, so the same clock time has a different surface form in each language. subtractive: «без N» / 'N to', which the v3 run suggests is hard in both languages — this is the within-probe control that separates 'Russian time is hard' from 'this one construction is hard'. literal: digital times identical in both languages, which must score near 100% or the probe itself is broken. arithmetic: relative offsets. The English wording is the natural spoken English for that clock time, not a translation of the Russian form; that is the comparison we want."
  },
